; The track's `[p0]` reference is `:scope piece` bound but appears
; outside any enclosing piece — fires `cross_ref_outside_scope`. The
; vector match short-circuits at the first failed element, so the
; phrase declaration sitting at root (also outside any piece) does
; not contribute extra diagnostics here.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic
    :code cross_ref_outside_scope
    :path [track sequence]))
